    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-148311",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.64,$ $\\text{Var}[Y]=0.84,$ and $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.16.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X-Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]\\pm 2\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X-Y]=0.64+0.84-2\\cdot 0.16=1.16.\n$$",
